From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 18:32:31 +0800
Subject: core/session: streamed text in message reads, and a delta sync route

Text and reasoning deltas are live-only: the projection stores an empty block on *.started and
the full text on *.ended. So a read in between (page load, reconnect, returning to the app) got
an empty block and the deltas that followed were appended to it: the reply showed garbled until
the block ended (minutes for a long one). LiveContent keeps what has been published of each open
block in memory, Session.messages / message / messageSync fill it in, and each delta event
carries the offset it starts at, so a client can drop what a read already gave it and refetch
when it missed some. Cleared after the *.ended projection and with the step's end.

GET /api/session/:id/message-sync?from&since&include&held lists every message from `from` (or
the newest `limit`) to the newest with its update time, and sends data only for what changed
since the client's watermark (10 s margin), unfinished steps, `include`d ids, and everything
older than `held`. One statement, so ids and data are one snapshot; `reset` when `from` is gone.

Ocelot-Patch: core/message-sync

